{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cght87FRevFpwubUtBXn1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I get **Dq ≈ 2660 cm⁻¹, B ≈ 529 cm⁻¹ and C ≈ 3000 cm⁻¹**. Dq and B are exact within the model. C is an estimate: I used an approximate ²E expression instead of diagonalising the full ²E matrix.\n\n**1. Dq from the ⁴T₂ band**\n\nFor octahedral d³, the transition ⁴A₂g → ⁴T₂g has energy 10Dq.\n- 10Dq = 26 600 cm⁻¹, so Dq = 2660 cm⁻¹.\n\n**2. B from the ⁴T₁ band**\n\nThe ⁴T₁g(F) energy above ⁴A₂g is:\n\nE = 15Dq + 7.5B − ½√(100Dq² − 180DqB + 225B²)\n\n- Setting E = 32 500 cm⁻¹ and 15Dq = 39 900 cm⁻¹ gives √(…) = 15B + 14 800.\n- Squaring both sides gives 707.56×10⁶ − 478 800B = 444 000B + 219.04×10⁶.\n- Solving: B = 488.52×10⁶ / 922 800 = 529 cm⁻¹.\n\nThis is about 58% of the free-ion value for Cr³⁺ (B₀ ≈ 918 cm⁻¹), which is typical for cyanide.\n\n**3. C from the ²E band**\n\nI used the strong-field approximation for the ²E energy:\n\nE(²E) ≈ 9B + 3C − 90B²/(10Dq)\n\n- 9B = 4765 cm⁻¹.\n- 90B²/(10Dq) = 948 cm⁻¹.\n- Setting E(²E) = 12 820 cm⁻¹ gives 3C = 12 820 − 4765 + 948 = 9004 cm⁻¹, so C ≈ 3000 cm⁻¹.\n\nThis gives C/B ≈ 5.7. The approximation leaves out higher-order mixing among the four ²E states, so C is uncertain by roughly ±100 cm⁻¹.\n\n{\"Dq\": 2660, \"B\": 529, \"C\": 3000, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Dq from 4T2, B from exact 4T1 formula, C from approximate strong-field 2E expression.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":817,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":817,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b115f4de-c6fc-4930-b086-eef5f7883b74","uuid":"6379c8b6-95d8-